information because the name of the

113
00:08:44.759 --> 00:08:47.929
function that we want to force
the model to call is information.

114
00:08:50.580 --> 00:08:51.440
After that we can try it out.

115
00:08:53.750 --> 00:08:57.659
So let's try it out on a simple sentence,

116
00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:13.220
His mom is Martha.

117
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:14.820
So now there's two people here.

118
00:09:15.639 --> 00:09:19.639
And we can see that what it
extracts is name Joe, age 30.

119
00:09:20.179 --> 00:09:30.779
Gets a second person this
time, name Martha, age 0.

120
00:09:31.559 --> 00:09:33.039
Which probably we can do better.

121
00:09:33.240 --> 00:09:35.580
We can force the model to
respond in a more educated way.

122
00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:39.100
And so what we're going to do
is we're going to add a prompt

123
00:09:39.100 --> 00:09:40.899
that's going to tell the
language model to do that.

124
00:09:41.980 --> 00:09:47.039
So now we're adding a prompt and we have
a system message where we say extract the

125
00:09:47.039 --> 00:09:50.620
relevant information if not explicitly
provided do not guess extract partial info.

126
00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.159
So hopefully what this
should do is this should force

127
00:09:54.159 --> 00:09:56.210
the language model or
this should allow the

128
00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.519
language model to not
respond always with an age

129
00:09:58.519 --> 00:10:01.080
it's not going to make
up this age equals zero.

130
00:10:01.700 --> 00:10:09.460
So we can create a new
extraction chain as this prompt,

131
00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:11.200
and then the extraction model.

132
00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:19.139
And if we call this
extraction chain on the same thing,

133
00:10:19.139 --> 00:10:22.440
we can now see that in the
arguments, we have name Martha,

134
00:10:22.440 --> 00:10:25.200
and there's nothing mentioned
about age so it's correctly reasoning

135
00:10:25.200 --> 00:10:27.950
that it doesn't need to
pass in information about age.

136
00:10:28.929 --> 00:10:31.610
Again we can probably do
better than just this AI message

137
00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:33.809
we can try to parse it
into some structure.

138
00:10:34.629 --> 00:10:39.190
So let's add back in that JSON
output parser that we had before.

139
00:10:40.110 --> 00:10:40.950
If we call it again, we can
see that it's parsed into this

